  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p28-q9-stem",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A red box contains two red and two blue marbles, and a blue box contains two red and two blue marbles. A marble is first drawn from the red box and its colour is noted. Subsequent marbles are drawn according to the following rules:",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p28-q9-rule-i",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "(I) If a red marble is drawn, it is returned to the red box, and the next marble is drawn from the red box.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p28-q9-rule-ii",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "(II) If a blue marble is drawn, it is returned to the blue box, and the next marble is drawn from the blue box.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p28-q9-instruction",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Find the probability that:",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the first marble is red",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac12$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(R_1)&=\\frac24\\\\P(R_1)&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the first marble is blue",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac12$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(B_1)&=\\frac24\\\\P(B_1)&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the second marble is red",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac9{20}$",
          "worked": "After a first red marble, the red box still contains two red and two blue marbles. After a first blue marble, the blue box contains two red and three blue marbles.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(R_2)&=\\frac12\\times\\frac24+\\frac12\\times\\frac25\\\\P(R_2)&=\\frac14+\\frac15\\\\P(R_2)&=\\frac9{20}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "the second marble is blue.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{11}{20}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(B_2)&=1-P(R_2)\\\\P(B_2)&=1-\\frac9{20}\\\\P(B_2)&=\\frac{11}{20}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q9-final-group",
        "type": "group",
        "label": null,
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p29-q9-continuation-text",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Eventually, each box will contain marbles of only one colour.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p29-continuation-e",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "e",
            "prompt": "Find the shortest number of steps required for this to happen.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "4 steps.\n\nEach of the four marbles initially in the wrong box must be transferred.",
              "worked": "Two blue marbles must move from the red box to the blue box, and two red marbles must move from the blue box to the red box. Each draw transfers at most one of these marbles, so at least four steps are required. The colour sequence $B,R,B,R$ transfers all four in four steps.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 22
          },
          {
            "id": "p29-continuation-f",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "f",
            "prompt": "Find the probability that this happens in the shortest number of steps.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac1{100}$.\n\nMultiply the probabilities along the required colour sequence $B,R,B,R$.",
              "worked": "Every draw must transfer a marble to its matching box. Starting from the red box, the only possible four-step colour sequence is $B,R,B,R$. The successive required probabilities are $\\frac24$, $\\frac25$, $\\frac14$ and $\\frac15$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{four steps})&=\\frac24\\times\\frac25\\times\\frac14\\times\\frac15\\\\P(\\text{four steps})&=\\frac1{100}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 30
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
